*> What each statement does with its operands.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  A                   PIC 9(4).
01  B                   PIC 9(4).
01  C                   PIC 9(4).
01  T                   PIC X(20).
01  P                   PIC 9(4).
01  IX                  PIC 9(4).
01  TBL.
    05  ROW             PIC X OCCURS 10.
01  FLAG                PIC X.
    88  DONE            VALUE "Y".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    MOVE A TO B C
    ADD A TO B GIVING C
    ADD A TO B
    SUBTRACT A FROM B
    MULTIPLY A BY B
    DIVIDE A INTO B
    DIVIDE A BY B GIVING C REMAINDER P
    COMPUTE C = A + B
    INITIALIZE T REPLACING ALPHANUMERIC BY SPACES
    SET IX UP BY A
    SET DONE TO TRUE
    SET IX TO A
    ACCEPT T
    DISPLAY T UPON CONSOLE
    STRING T DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO T WITH POINTER P
    UNSTRING T DELIMITED BY SPACE INTO A B COUNT IN C TALLYING IN P
    INSPECT T TALLYING A FOR ALL "X"
    INSPECT T REPLACING ALL "X" BY "Y"
    CALL "SUB" USING A BY CONTENT B RETURNING C
    PERFORM VARYING IX FROM A BY B UNTIL IX > C
        MOVE ROW(IX) TO FLAG
    END-PERFORM
    IF A > B MOVE A TO C END-IF
    MOVE LENGTH OF T TO A
    STOP RUN.
